  "name": "Repeat forever",
  "kind": "solids",
  "blurb": "A grid of copies to the horizon, each turned, stretched and tinted by a list",
  "layout": "linear",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "slug": "note",
      "pos": {
        "x": 40.0,
        "y": 40.0
      },
      "controls": {},
      "options": {},
      "values": {
        "text": {
          "Text": "One rounded box, repeated on a grid that goes on forever: the Repeat folds every point into one cell, so endless copies cost what one does. Three Random lists on its Per copy rows turn, stretch and tint each copy; a Forever repeat runs through a list cell by cell, each row shifted by one, so lists of different lengths never line up the same way twice. The Ground after the Repeat is not repeated, since a modifier changes only what is cabled into it. Try another Seed on a list, or Render 3D's Lens Type on Fisheye."
        }
      },
      "width": 380.0
    },
